<title>FRANCE: Cr Foncier sells property development unit.</title>
<headline>Cr Foncier sells property development unit.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Credit Foncier  said on Thursday that it had sold the property development activities of its Foncier Habitat subsidiary to Highridge Partners of the United States.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that Highridge Partners had purchased Foncier Habitat's interests in Marignan Immobilier, Rocamar, Foncier Habitat Promotion and Provestim. The sale terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Credit Foncier, a state-controlled property lender that suffered 10.75 billion francs of losses in 1995 before returning to profit last year, said the deal formed part of its strategy to focus on its core businesses.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
